@server_HostAddress = http://localhost:5259
@token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
@resourceId = YOUR_RESOURCE_ID_HERE
@snippetId = YOUR_SNIPPET_ID_HERE
@taskId = YOUR_TASK_ID_HERE

### 1. Health Check
GET {{server_HostAddress}}/api/health
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Register New User
POST {{server_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "alex",
  "email": "alex@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### 3. Login User (Copy the token from the response into @token above)
POST {{server_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alex@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### 4. Get Current User Profile (Protected)
GET {{server_HostAddress}}/api/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RESOURCES  (Developer Bookmarks)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 5. Create a Resource (Protected)
POST {{server_HostAddress}}/api/resources
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "React Documentation",
  "url": "https://react.dev",
  "notes": "Official guide for React 19 features and hooks",
  "type": "docs"
}

###

### 6. Get All My Resources (Protected)
GET {{server_HostAddress}}/api/resources
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 7. Get Single Resource by ID (Protected — paste an ID from step 6 into @resourceId)
GET {{server_HostAddress}}/api/resources/{{resourceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 8. Update Resource by ID (Protected)
PUT {{server_HostAddress}}/api/resources/{{resourceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "React 19 Official Documentation",
  "url": "https://react.dev/learn",
  "notes": "Updated: covers React 19 compiler, actions, and server components",
  "type": "docs"
}

###

### 9. Delete Resource by ID (Protected)
DELETE {{server_HostAddress}}/api/resources/{{resourceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SNIPPETS  (Reusable Code Snippets)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 10. Create a Snippet (Protected)
POST {{server_HostAddress}}/api/snippets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "EF Core SQLite Setup",
  "description": "Register AppDbContext with SQLite in Program.cs",
  "code": "builder.Services.AddDbContext<AppDbContext>(options =>\n    options.UseSqlite(\"Data Source=devshelf.db\"));",
  "language": "csharp",
  "tags": "dotnet,efcore,sqlite"
}

###

### 11. Get All My Snippets (Protected)
GET {{server_HostAddress}}/api/snippets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 12. Get Single Snippet by ID (Protected — paste an ID from step 11 into @snippetId)
GET {{server_HostAddress}}/api/snippets/{{snippetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 13. Update Snippet by ID (Protected)
PUT {{server_HostAddress}}/api/snippets/{{snippetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "EF Core SQLite Setup (Updated)",
  "description": "Updated setup with environment-based connection string",
  "code": "var conn = builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString(\"Default\");\nbuilder.Services.AddDbContext<AppDbContext>(o => o.UseSqlite(conn));",
  "language": "csharp",
  "tags": "dotnet,efcore"
}

###

### 14. Delete Snippet by ID (Protected)
DELETE {{server_HostAddress}}/api/snippets/{{snippetId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TASKS  (Developer Task List)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 15. Create a Task (Protected)
POST {{server_HostAddress}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Build React frontend",
  "description": "Scaffold Vite app, set up Axios and AuthContext",
  "status": "todo",
  "priority": "high",
  "project": "DevShelf"
}

###

### 16. Get All My Tasks (Protected — optionally filter by status)
GET {{server_HostAddress}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 16b. Get Tasks filtered by status (Protected)
GET {{server_HostAddress}}/api/tasks?status=todo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 17. Get Single Task by ID (Protected — paste an ID from step 16 into @taskId)
GET {{server_HostAddress}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 18. Update Task Status only — PATCH (Protected)
PATCH {{server_HostAddress}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "in-progress"
}

###

### 19. Update Full Task — PUT (Protected)
PUT {{server_HostAddress}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Build React frontend & Axios service",
  "description": "Scaffold Vite app, configure Axios, implement AuthContext and protected routes",
  "status": "done",
  "priority": "high",
  "project": "DevShelf"
}

###

### 20. Delete Task by ID (Protected)
DELETE {{server_HostAddress}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
